I can help with that. To proceed, I need to locate your current reservation and confirm the changes. Changing the destination from Los Angeles to Las Vegas is a change of destination, which isn’t a simple flight modification and typically requires canceling the existing itinerary and rebooking a new ATL→LAS nonstop itinerary for the same travel date(s). If any portion has already flown, we can’t modify and would need to escalate to a human agent. Refunds to the original payment method generally take 5–7 business days after cancellation. Travel insurance would be 30 USD per passenger if you choose it for the new booking. Please provide:
1) your airline user ID;
2) your reservation ID (if known) – otherwise I can help locate it using your name and travel date;
3) number of passengers (1–5);
4) preferred cabin class (basic_economy, economy, or business);
5) travel dates for the ATL→LAS trip (outbound and inbound if this is a round trip);
6) whether you want travel insurance for the new booking;
7) any flight time preferences.
Once I have these, I’ll present a concrete plan and ask you to confirm with a simple 'Yes' to proceed with cancellation and rebooking.

